Subject: [PATCH 12/36] B70-QSA-T03: QSA XPU microbench + sweep, profiler
 bucket summary

- benchmarks/kernels/bench_qwen4_qsa_xpu.py: every QSA op per sparse layer at
  the TP4 Flash-Next shape (6q/1kv/256; indexer 4x128, ratio 4, 2048+3) through
  the real entry points: decode scorer, native and torch top-k, select
  decode/prefill, prefill scorer, expand, sparse GQA (+merge). Decode rows
  8/32/64 (DFlash K=7 verify), prefill one 4096-row chunk, ctx 4K..256K,
  page-table width from --max-model-len (as the engine sizes decode logits).
  Torch reference checks (tie-tolerant selection, attention max abs).
  Per launched kernel: n_regs, n_spills, threads/warp, DPAS / 2D block IO in
  the TTGIR. --graph times decode as XPU-graph replays. --sweep <kernel> runs
  a grid through B70_QSA_TUNE (same hook as the engine) and the env knobs;
  --budget sums per-layer cost x 12 against the W1 sparse-dense gap. SYCL bar
  (W1 azk/Strata) is printed next to each matching row.
- benchmarks/kernels/qsa_profile_summary.py: buckets a vLLM torch-profiler
  trace by QSA op / dense piece, device busy vs host gaps, per step.
- b70_qsa_tune/: step-trace lib rebuild for the 0.32 venv, one-change engine
  arm generator, four-card parallel job runner.
- tests: B70_QSA_TUNE validation.
