+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+"""B70-QSA-T: per-kernel microbench + launch-config sweep for Qwen4Exp QSA on Intel XPU.
+
+Times every QSA op the engine runs per sparse layer, at the TP4 shape of
+Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on one Arc Pro B70 (6 q heads / 1 KV head / head_dim 256;
+indexer 4 heads x 128, compress ratio 4, top 2048 tokens = 512 blocks + 3 tail;
+BF16), through the real vLLM entry points, with a torch reference check:
+
+  decode_score   _qsa_mqa_paged_uniform_kernel (decode/verify scorer)
+  topk_native    torch.ops._C.top_k_per_row_decode (vllm-xpu-kernels SYCL)
+  topk_torch     _qsa_topk_torch (deterministic int64-key path, B70-QSA-09 chunks)
+  select_decode  scorer + top-k as qsa_select_paged_decode runs them
+  prefill_score  _qsa_mqa_paged_prefill_kernel (one 4096-row chunk)
+  select_prefill scorer + top-k as qsa_select_paged_prefill runs them
+  expand         _expand_qsa_indices_kernel
+  attn           _qsa_sparse_paged_gqa_splitk_kernel (+ _qsa_merge_splitk_kernel)
+
+Decode rows are requests x DECODE_QUERY_LEN (8 = one DFlash K=7 verify step), so
+rows 8/32/64 = 1/4/8 requests; prefill is one request's 4096-row chunk at the
+end of its context. The decode logits width is the page-table width, i.e.
+--max-model-len / 4 (65,728 columns at 262,144 with an 832-token block), not the
+context: that is how the engine runs it (see H1 in the run's C-tuning-prep.md).
+
+Every timed row also prints, per Triton kernel it launched, the compiled
+kernel's register count, spill bytes, threads per warp and whether the TTGIR
+carries a DPAS layout / 2D block loads, so a slow config can be read before it
+is tuned.
+
+Usage (one card; --card picks it with ZE_AFFINITY_MASK semantics):
+  python benchmarks/kernels/bench_qwen4_qsa_xpu.py --ops all --out qsa_bench.jsonl
+  python benchmarks/kernels/bench_qwen4_qsa_xpu.py --sweep sparse_gqa_prefill --ctx 32768
+  python benchmarks/kernels/bench_qwen4_qsa_xpu.py --sweep decode_score --rows 8 --ctx 4096,131072
+  python benchmarks/kernels/bench_qwen4_qsa_xpu.py --budget   # per-step totals vs the W1 dense gap
+
+Overrides use the same mechanism as the engine (B70_QSA_TUNE, see
+vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_xpu_tuning.py), so a winning sweep row is
+a B70_QSA_TUNE line for an engine def unchanged.
+"""
+
